# 4. Layered Defense Summary & Hardening Checklist

## 4.1 How the Technologies Fit Together

```
HARDWARE & FIRMWARE:  TPM 2.0 / Pluton · UEFI Secure Boot · Measured Boot · IOMMU/Kernel DMA Protection · SMM/DRTM
HYPERVISOR (VBS):     VTL1 Secure Kernel · HVCI (W^X kernel, driver blocklist) · Credential Guard (LsaIso)
KERNEL / OS CORE:     SRM access checks · Tokens + MIC integrity levels · PatchGuard · DSE · PPL (LSASS) 
IDENTITY:             Kerberos > NTLM · Windows Hello for Business / FIDO2 · Entra ID + Conditional Access · LAPS
EXECUTION CONTROL:    WDAC/App Control · AppLocker · Smart App Control · Exploit Protection (DEP/ASLR/CFG/CET)
ENDPOINT PROTECTION:  Defender AV · ASR rules · Network Protection · Controlled Folder Access · EDR · Tamper Protection
DATA PROTECTION:      BitLocker (TPM+PIN) · DPAPI · EFS · recovery key escrow
ADMIN HYGIENE:        UAC (AAM) · least privilege · tiered admin · Protected Users · auditing/SIEM
```

## 4.2 Baseline Hardening Checklist

- [ ] Secure Boot + TPM 2.0 enabled; UEFI password set; boot order locked
- [ ] BitLocker with **TPM + PIN** (XTS-AES 256 where policy requires), recovery keys escrowed (AD/Entra)
- [ ] **VBS + HVCI (Memory Integrity)** enabled; incompatible drivers remediated; Vulnerable Driver Blocklist on
- [ ] **Credential Guard** enabled (UEFI lock for high-value endpoints); LSA Protection (`RunAsPPL`) on
- [ ] WDigest disabled; NTLMv1/LM disabled (`LmCompatibilityLevel=5`); SMB signing required; SMBv1 removed; LDAP signing + channel binding
- [ ] UAC enabled at default or higher; no `LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy=1`; daily-use accounts are standard users
- [ ] Windows LAPS deployed for local administrator passwords
- [ ] ASR rules in Block (after Audit tuning); Network Protection + Controlled Folder Access on; Tamper Protection on
- [ ] Exploit Protection system defaults (DEP/ASLR/CFG/SEHOP) + per-app hardening for Office, PDF readers, browsers
- [ ] WDAC/App Control base policy (audit → enforce) with recommended block rules; AppLocker only if needed
- [ ] Windows Hello for Business / FIDO2 passkeys rolled out; legacy password-only sign-in reduced
- [ ] Advanced Audit Policy configured (logon, process creation 4688 with command line, object access, privilege use, policy change); logs forwarded to SIEM (also Sysmon)
- [ ] Patch management (monthly cumulative updates; WSUS/Intune rings); remove unnecessary features (PowerShell v2, SMB1, legacy protocols)
- [ ] Benchmarks applied: Microsoft Security Baselines (via Security Compliance Toolkit), CIS Benchmarks, DISA STIGs

